  <Placemark>
   <name>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 19 at 1:50PM CDT until September 19 at 2:30PM CDT by NWS Birmingham AL</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>SVRBMX

The National Weather Service in Birmingham has issued a

* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...
Southwestern Lee County in east central Alabama...
Northeastern Macon County in southeastern Alabama...

* Until 230 PM CDT.

* At 150 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Tuskegee
National Forest, or near Auburn, moving south at 15 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

* Locations impacted include...
Auburn, Society Hill, Tuskegee National Forest, I 85 Rest Area, and
Chewacla State Park.</Snippet>
