  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued September 19 at 10:59AM EDT until September 24 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Northern Indiana</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in
Indiana...Ohio...

Wabash River near Bluffton IN affecting Wells County.

Saint Marys River at St. Mary's River near Fort Wayne affecting
Allen IN County.

Saint Marys River near Decatur affecting Allen IN, Adams and Van
Wert Counties.

...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Indiana...

Wabash River near Linn Grove affecting Wells and Adams Counties.

For the Wabash River...including Linn Grove, Bluffton IN, Wabash,
Logansport...Moderate flooding is forecast.
For the Saint Marys River...including Decatur, St. Mary's River near
Fort Wayne...Moderate flooding is forecast.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...Saint Marys River at St. Mary's River near Fort Wayne.

* WHEN...Until Thursday evening.

* IMPACTS...At 15.0 feet, Flooding occurs on the lowest unprotected
city streets, park drives and county roads.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 10:30 AM EDT Saturday the stage was 14.8 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 16.4 feet
tomorrow evening. It will then fall below flood stage Wednesday
evening.
- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
