   <name>Flood Warning issued September 19 at 10:54AM EDT until September 20 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Wilmington OH</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The National Weather Service in Wilmington has issued a Flood
Warning for the following rivers...

St. Marys River at Rockford.

Additional information is available at www.weather.gov/iln.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...St. Marys River at Rockford.

* WHEN...From this afternoon to Sunday evening.

* IMPACTS...At 13.0 feet, State Route 117 near Route 118 north of
Rockford is water-covered and closed.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 10:40 AM EDT Saturday the stage was 12.9 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage this
afternoon to a crest of 13.2 feet this evening. It will then fall
below flood stage early tomorrow afternoon.
- Flood stage is 13.0 feet.</Snippet>
