   <name>Gale Warning issued September 19 at 6:43AM AKDT until September 20 at 1:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_moderate</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the first Small Craft Advisory, south winds 25 to
30 kt with gusts up to 35 kt and seas 8 to 13 ft expected. For
the Gale Warning, south winds 30 to 35 kt with gusts up to 45
kt and seas 16 to 21 ft expected. For the second Small Craft
Advisory, south winds 25 to 30 kt with gusts up to 40 kt and
seas 18 to 21 ft expected. For the third Small Craft Advisory,
southwest winds 20 to 25 kt with gusts up to 35 kt and seas 14
to 19 ft expected.

* WHERE...Cape Edgecumbe to Cape Spencer from 15 to 80 NM.

* WHEN...For the first Small Craft Advisory, from 7 PM this
evening to 1 AM AKDT Sunday. For the Gale Warning, from 1 AM
to 1 PM AKDT Sunday. For the second Small Craft Advisory, from
1 PM to 6 PM AKDT Sunday. For the third Small Craft Advisory,
from 7 PM Sunday to 6 AM AKDT Monday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.</Snippet>
