   <name>Flood Warning issued September 19 at 9:16AM CDT until September 20 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS La Crosse WI</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Fayette County in northeastern Iowa...

* WHEN...Until 700 AM CDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying
and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads
remain closed due to flooding.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 912 AM CDT, local law enforcement and automated gauges
indicated that flooding continues across the county this morning
due to 3 to 6 inches of rain that occurred last night, with the
flooding impacts becoming more concentrated along the Turkey and
Viola rivers moving into the afternoon and overnight.
- Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches are possible in the
warned area this afternoon and evening.
- Some locations experiencing flooding include...
West Union, Fayette, Elgin, Clermont, Maynard, Hawkeye,
Arlington, Waucoma, Wadena, Westgate, St. Lucas, Randalia,
Donnan, Douglas, Albany, Volga River State Park, Highway 93 And
County W 14, County Roads W 42 And B 40, Eldorado and Brainard.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
