   <name>Small Craft Advisory issued September 19 at 2:23AM PDT until September 21 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Medford OR</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_minor</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, north winds 20 to 25 kt
with gusts up to 30 kt and seas 5 to 9 ft at 5 to 6 seconds
expected. For the Hazardous Seas Watch, north winds 20 to 30 kt
with gusts up to 35 kt and very steep and hazardous seas 7 to 10
ft at 5 to 6 seconds possible.

* WHERE...Small Craft Advisory for all of the area late this
evening through Monday evening, except a Hazardous Seas Watch
from Gold Beach to Pt. St. George during Monday afternoon and
evening.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, from 11 PM this evening
to 11 PM PDT Monday. For the Hazardous Seas Watch, from Monday
afternoon through Monday evening.

* IMPACTS...Very steep and hazardous seas could capsize or
damage vessels. Bar crossing could become especially hazardous.

* View the hazard area in detail at https://go.usa.gov/x6hks</Snippet>
